OVERVIEW: Add empty virtual groups (alias of create-groups)

Adds one or more virtual groups to the Xcode project. This is an alias of the
create-groups command.

Examples:
  xcodeproj-cli add-group UI/Components Services/API
  xcodeproj-cli add-group Architecture/Models Architecture/Views

USAGE: xcodeproj-cli add-group [--project <project>] [--workspace <workspace>] [--verbose] [--dry-run] <group-paths> ...

ARGUMENTS:
  <group-paths>           One or more group paths to create

OPTIONS:
  -p, --project <project> Path to .xcodeproj file (default: looks for
                          *.xcodeproj in current directory)
  -w, --workspace <workspace>
                          Path to .xcworkspace file
  -V, --verbose           Enable verbose output with performance metrics
  --dry-run               Preview changes without saving
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

